WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.288 --> 00:00:03.038
(dramatic music)

00:00:04.227 --> 00:00:06.968
- When I tell people I'm
a pro-foosball player

00:00:06.968 --> 00:00:10.551
there's always a look
of like astonishment.

00:00:11.768 --> 00:00:13.357
I get laughter sometimes too,

00:00:13.357 --> 00:00:16.387
what, I didn't know there was
tournaments for that, foosball?

00:00:16.387 --> 00:00:18.861
Yeah that's the one
that's, that's what I do.

00:00:18.861 --> 00:00:21.611
(dramatic music)

00:00:26.124 --> 00:00:29.336
Foosball's not just a, a barroom game.

00:00:29.336 --> 00:00:32.503
It's a competitive sport that's played

00:00:33.688 --> 00:00:38.157
at a professional level by
people all around the world.

00:00:38.157 --> 00:00:40.460
It's like a hand-to-hand combat, you're,

00:00:40.460 --> 00:00:41.942
you're standing this close you know,

00:00:41.942 --> 00:00:44.471
you're standing three feet
away from your opponent,

00:00:44.471 --> 00:00:46.903
and it's almost like you're in a fight,

00:00:46.903 --> 00:00:49.820
you're battling against each other.

00:00:54.466 --> 00:00:58.114
I come from a, a long
line of foosball players.

00:00:58.114 --> 00:01:00.236
I got into foosball because of my dad.

00:01:00.236 --> 00:01:03.444
He played in the, the golden era,

00:01:03.444 --> 00:01:06.796
the 1970s when there was
a million dollar tour.

00:01:06.796 --> 00:01:08.887
I've been playing for 20 years now.

00:01:08.887 --> 00:01:12.695
So for the first 10 to
12 years of my career

00:01:12.695 --> 00:01:15.554
I would practice on a table at home.

00:01:15.554 --> 00:01:17.175
It would be complete repetition.

00:01:17.175 --> 00:01:18.988
Over and over and over.

00:01:18.988 --> 00:01:22.754
Every player in here can
execute a shot or a pass.

00:01:22.754 --> 00:01:27.351
But it's a matter of
constructing a solid game plan.

00:01:27.351 --> 00:01:30.606
It's like a, a game of
chess on the mental side.

00:01:30.606 --> 00:01:33.221
It, it could be pretty taxing.

00:01:33.221 --> 00:01:35.738
Physically by the end of the weekend you,

00:01:35.738 --> 00:01:38.053
you're sore, your hands are sore,

00:01:38.053 --> 00:01:41.519
your feet are sore so you
have to be in decent shape.

00:01:41.519 --> 00:01:43.621
I always got a, a sweat band on my arm

00:01:43.621 --> 00:01:45.599
just in case I get into a, a heated match

00:01:45.599 --> 00:01:48.432
I gotta, you know, wipe my brow, so.

00:01:50.778 --> 00:01:54.195
I go to the World Cup, which is basically

00:01:55.248 --> 00:01:59.415
our version of the Olympics,
and I compete on Team USA.

00:02:00.464 --> 00:02:02.064
I do believe it should be in the Olympics.

00:02:02.064 --> 00:02:05.231
Our only problem is the fact that

00:02:05.231 --> 00:02:08.912
there's not a standardized foosball table.

00:02:08.912 --> 00:02:10.995
And I'll do whatever it takes to,

00:02:10.995 --> 00:02:14.918
for the sport to reach that next level.

00:02:14.918 --> 00:02:16.316
Bottom line is it makes me happy

00:02:16.316 --> 00:02:19.899
that this is what I do
and, yeah I love it.

